<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><ncx xmlns="http://www.daisy.org/z3986/2005/ncx/" version="2005-1" xml:lang="en"><head><meta name="dtb:uid" content="urn:uuid:230a4d06-edaa-43e8-ae46-d3bb10f4859e"/><meta name="dtb:depth" content="2"/><meta name="dtb:totalPageCount" content="0"/><meta name="dtb:maxPageNumber" content="0"/></head><docTitle><text>Banking on Oil</text></docTitle><navMap><navPoint id="nav-1" playOrder="1"><navLabel><text>Introduction: following the money in oil</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch001.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-2" playOrder="2"><navLabel><text>1. Who pays for an oil cargo before you do?</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml"/><navPoint id="nav-3" playOrder="3"><navLabel><text>The bank is waiting for the next buyer’s money</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-the-bank-is-waiting-for-the-next-buyers-money"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-4" playOrder="4"><navLabel><text>Credit terms can reach into the sale</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-credit-terms-can-reach-into-the-sale"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-5" playOrder="5"><navLabel><text>The cargo arrives before the paperwork</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-the-cargo-arrives-before-the-paperwork"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-6" playOrder="6"><navLabel><text>The contract decides who carries the payment gap</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-the-contract-decides-who-carries-the-payment-gap"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-7" playOrder="7"><navLabel><text>A profitable trader can still need more cash</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-a-profitable-trader-can-still-need-more-cash"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-8" playOrder="8"><navLabel><text>Borrowing capacity is part of the business</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-borrowing-capacity-is-part-of-the-business"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-9" playOrder="9"><navLabel><text>Sources and method</text></navLabel><content src="t