-and-documentary-references"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-71" playOrder="71"><navLabel><text>8. Can a credit squeeze disrupt oil supplies?</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml"/><navPoint id="nav-72" playOrder="72"><navLabel><text>The cargo and the cash run on different clocks</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-the-cargo-and-the-cash-run-on-different-clocks"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-73" playOrder="73"><navLabel><text>The same funding buys fewer barrels</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-the-same-funding-buys-fewer-barrels"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-74" playOrder="74"><navLabel><text>Who can take over the delivery?</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-who-can-take-over-the-delivery"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-75" playOrder="75"><navLabel><text>The financial system absorbed much of the 2022 shock</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-the-financial-system-absorbed-much-of-the-2022-shock"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-76" playOrder="76"><navLabel><text>Uniper had an economic loss to absorb</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-uniper-had-an-economic-loss-to-absorb"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-77" playOrder="77"><navLabel><text>Standby credit has a maturity too</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-standby-credit-has-a-maturity-too"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-78" playOrder="78"><navLabel><text>More detailed safeguards, with a defined scope</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-more-detailed-safeguards-with-a-defined-scope"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-79" playOrder="79"><navLabel><text>Testing the whole delivery chain</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-testing-the-whole-delivery-chain"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-80" playOrder="80"><navLabel><text>Sources and documentary references</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-sources-and-documentary-references"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-81" playO